        <mxCell id="cons" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;fontSize=10;align=left;spacing=8;" value="Statistical consequences:&lt;br&gt;• the loss VALUE is scale-stable (÷ N) — no spikes just because a batch contains long games&lt;br&gt;• the GRADIENT averages over a varying N → effective batch size and gradient variance fluctuate between learner steps&lt;br&gt;• within a batch every step weighs equally → a game’s influence is proportional to its length (a 120-step game counts 3× a 40-step game)&lt;br&gt;• trajectories are drawn without replacement within a batch, but independently across learner steps (a trajectory is typically reused many times before FIFO eviction)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="690" x="770" y="760" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
